# Feeds come from a self-hosted FreshRSS over its Google Reader API, so the
# server address and the account are facts about one machine's own network. This
# repo is public and carries neither.
#
# The backticks are newsboat's shell evaluation, documented in `man newsboat`
# under Shell Evaluation: the command runs and its output becomes the value.
# `install/flags.yml` declares both variables, so `dotfiles check` fails while
# either is unset.
#
# Quoted rather than bare, because the two forms differ only when the variable is
# unset. Bare leaves the line with too few parameters and newsboat refuses to
# start. Quoted, it prints `You must set freshrss-url to use FreshRSS` and starts
# anyway, so a machine with no FreshRSS to reach still gets a reader.
#
# `FRESHRSS_URL` is the web app's address, which the rss launcher opens. Newsboat
# logs in at its Google Reader API endpoint, a path under that address.
#
# The password sits in the desk's keyring under service `freshrss`, so it is in no
# file and no process's environment. `secret-tool` answers on Linux and `security`
# on macOS, whose keychain refuses a session with no window server, such as ssh.
urls-source "freshrss"
freshrss-url "`echo ${FRESHRSS_URL:+$FRESHRSS_URL/api/greader.php}`"
freshrss-login "`echo $FRESHRSS_LOGIN`"
freshrss-passwordeval "secret-tool lookup service freshrss 2>/dev/null || security find-generic-password -s freshrss -w"
refresh-on-startup yes
